<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gavril Krastevich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1898</span> · Also known as Gavril Pasha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gavril Krastevich was a Bulgarian scholar and Ottoman official who served as governor-general of Eastern Rumelia from 1884 to 1885. His administration was overthrown by the bloodless coup of September 1885 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plovdiv">Plovdiv</a>, which united Eastern Rumelia with the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Earlier he had worked for an independent Bulgarian church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gavril-krastevich.jpg" alt="Gavril Krastevich" width="320" height="489" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitar Kavra · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gavril_Krastevich_General_Governor_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
